==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.67~20 seconds<sup>20f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.67~20 seconds<sup>20f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 2~20 seconds<sup>60f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gory|Gories]] spawn, delay 2~20 seconds<sup>60f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Bore]] spawns as the boss.

==Strategy==
It's mandatory to have all treasures from [[Empire of Cats]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] before trying this stage. [[Into the Future]]'s anti-Red treasures are also recommended, but not necessary. Similarly to [[One Horn]], Bore is a short-ranged pusher, except with much higher stats and speed that necessitate the use of [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|Crowd-Controllers]]. However, Bore is particularly vulnerable to the [[Slow]] debuff, as it will reduce his pushing power enough to nullify the threat he poses. [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Sorceress Cat]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]] are your main options for slowing him, but multiple of either unit are needed to consistently slow him. Another strategy is stacking several Bahamuts, but do note that this is very time consuming.

