==Trivia==
*''Carapaccio'' is a combination of the words ''carpaccio'' (an Italian dish consisting of raw meat or fish, thinly sliced and served with a sauce) and ''carapace'' (the upper exoskeleton of a number of aquatic animals such as turtles and prawns).

